                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On April 2, the Embassy in London reported information from the British Foreign
                    Office on the conversations of March 24 between Mr. Bevin and Generalissimo
                    Stalin at Moscow. Concerning their discussions on Iran, the Embassy cited Mr.
                    Bevin as stating “that the propaganda that Britain opposed an oil concession to
                    Russia was without foundation. The British Government, he explained, had no
                    objection to an oil concession being made to Russia so long as Iranian
                    independence was not affected. No comment of significance was made to this by
                    Stalin.” (telegram 2020, 741.61/4–247). The British record of the conversation
                    of March 24 is printed in <ref target="frus:frus1947v02/pg_278">volume II, page
                        278</ref>.</p>
            </div>
